---
name: competitive-analysis
description: Compare alternatives using decision-derived dimensions and evidence rather than feature lists.
license: MIT
---

Frame the decision and constraints first. Build comparison dimensions from the decision, not from marketing categories. Use primary documentation, hands-on evidence where available, and explicitly separate documented behavior from inference. For each alternative record capabilities, constraints, evidence, confidence, and consequences. Include negative results and a verdict: adopted, adapted, rejected, or deferred. Use the deep-research curiosity and bibliography-rationale rules.
